## Founding & History
Every Man & His Dog Vineyard is a small, family-run vineyard located in Tasmania's Coal River Valley, a short drive from Hobart. The vineyard, cellar door, and bed & breakfast were sold in November 2021 to new Hobart-based owners. The new owners plan to incorporate their other business into the vineyard. The vineyard is described as being "built on stories, connection, and doing things a little differently". It is situated amongst some of the oldest vineyards in the Coal Valley and is potentially the smallest commercial company operating in Tasmania.

## People
The current owners of Every Man & His Dog Vineyard are Hobart-based, having purchased the property in November 2021. Andrew and Loretta are mentioned as the owners who tell stories to visitors. Helen Curtis is noted as the co-owner and chocolate maker at Federation Artisan Chocolate, which is located on-site at the vineyard. The vineyard operates as a family business, with owners often on-site.

## Vineyard & Site
Every Man & His Dog Vineyard is located in Tasmania's Coal River Valley. The vineyard spans 2.3 hectares of land. It offers sweeping rural views and a peaceful atmosphere. The vineyard is set amongst some of the oldest vineyards in the Coal Valley. No reliable information found from public sources regarding elevation, aspect, soil type, or specific farming approach (conventional, organic, biodynamic).

## Cellar Door Experience
The cellar door at Every Man & His Dog Vineyard is described as relaxed, warm, and conversational, offering a personal and unhurried experience. It is open daily from 12 pm to 5 pm, with experiences bookable before midday. Visitors are welcomed and staff take time to discuss the wines, vineyard, and stories behind each bottle. The vineyard offers unique wine tasting experiences, including guided wine and chocolate pairings. Guests can enjoy a tour around the vineyard. Reservations are recommended to ensure a personalized experience.

## Food & Hospitality
Every Man & His Dog Vineyard is home to Federation Artisan Chocolate, which creates handcrafted chocolates designed to pair with their wines. They offer guided wine and chocolate pairing experiences. Visitors can also enjoy wood-fired pizzas, artisan cheese platters, and dessert flights. The vineyard provides a charming setting for events such as birthdays, celebrations, family reunions, and weddings. Chocolate making events are also available.

## Awards & Recognition
Every Man & His Dog Vineyard produces "award-winning wines". No specific awards, critic scores, or Halliday ratings were found in the search results.

## Sustainability & Certifications
No reliable information found from public sources regarding organic/biodynamic certification, sustainability practices, or water/energy approach.

## Visiting Practical Info
The vineyard is located in the Coal River Valley, just a short drive from Hobart, approximately 20 minutes by car. It is also described as being "a stone's throw from the historic town of Richmond".
Address: 1314 Richmond Road
Phone: (03) 6250 3435
Website: https://everymanandhisdogvineyard.com/
The vineyard is open from 12 pm to 5 pm daily, with experiences available to book prior to midday.

## Notable / Distinctive
Every Man & His Dog Vineyard is distinctive for being a small, family-run vineyard that integrates a bean-to-bar chocolate maker, Federation Artisan Chocolate, on-site. This allows for unique wine and chocolate pairing experiences that are not found elsewhere. The vineyard focuses on small-batch production (2,500–3,000 bottles annually) and offers classic alongside lesser-known and exotic varietals like Siegerrebe and Ehrenfelser. The cellar door experience is characterized by its personal, unhurried, and conversational approach, often involving the owners. The vineyard also offers a bed & breakfast.

